# Sellerboard -> Power BI, once a day, last 4 full days (server clock is UTC: 07:30 UTC = 13:00 IST).
# UK  (account Uk-AMZ)              -> powerbidb.Uk_breakdown_data              13:00 IST
# US  (account premiumcarproduct)   -> powerbidb.Sellerboard_breakdown_data_2024 13:30 IST (--us-premium)
# The 30-minute gap keeps the two runs apart: both use the same Sellerboard login and switch its account.
# `timeout -k 1m 20m` stops a hung run, so it can never overlap the next one. A failed run only writes
# its log and exits; it never stops the other job.
# Install with `crontab -e`, replacing older Sellerboard lines. Use absolute paths (`which uv`).
MAILTO=""
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< UK-Product-Breakdown-Data Start >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
30 7 * * * cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 20m /root/.local/bin/uv run --no-sync python run.py --uk-amazon --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< UK-Product-Breakdown-Data End >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< US-Premiumcarproduct Start >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
0 8 * * * cd /data/cron/UK-Product-Breakdown-Data && timeout -k 1m 20m /root/.local/bin/uv run --no-sync python run.py --us-premium --quiet >> logs/cron-output-us.log 2>&1
#<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< US-Premiumcarproduct End >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
